Hexagon HTP: HVX conv step, and the match of the state step on the real graph

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9, with patches 0001 and 0002 applied. This patch changes only
files of 0002 and adds one header.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h           new: the chain checks, with a reason for each failure
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp          uses the header, logs the first failed condition
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c        the conv step in HVX, no DMA and no VTCM

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/hexagon-fusion/0003-hexagon-htp-gdn-state-step-hvx-conv-and-match-fix.patch
    cmake --build build-snapdragon -j

Push to the phone: libggml-htp-v79.so (ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/), libggml-hexagon.so (bin/),
and test-backend-ops (bin/).

Problem 1: GDN_CONV_STEP took 350 us per op

The conv step of 0002 ran a scalar loop on data in VTCM. Scalar loads and stores to VTCM are
slow, and no other kernel of this backend does that. The new kernel is HVX only: it reads DDR
with unaligned vector loads, keeps a block of 32 channels in registers, and writes DDR with
unaligned vector stores. The layout change from 3 lanes per channel (the slot) to 4 lanes per
channel (the taps) uses rotates and masks, four vdeal ops split the block into tap planes, and
the four products are added in the order of the CPU reference. The SiLU is the sigmoid and the
multiply of the SILU op. The new slot lanes come back from the 4-lane block with rotates and
masks. Only d_conv = 4 is fused; another width keeps the unfused path.

Problem 2: GDN_STATE_STEP never matched on the real graph

The check "no reader of the state part of the output outside the chain" looked at the source
of each reader. A view node has the whole output as its source, thus the attention view of
the output (the first S_v * H floats) failed the check. The check now judges a view node by
its own range, and a compute node by the view it reads. A host probe that runs the same
checks on the one-token graph of Qwen3.5-2B matches 18 of 18 state chains and 18 of 18 conv
chains after the fix.

With GGML_HEXAGON_VERBOSE=1 the host logs one line for each candidate chain that does not
match, with the failed condition, for example:
    ggml-hex: HTP0 GDN_STATE_STEP candidate node_46 (node 46): the state part of the output has a reader outside the chain

